["line","r","$\\rho$ constant, at $a/2$ on the disc and $2$, $3$ and $4\\,a$ outside"],["line","surface","the rim of the disc, $\\rho = a$, a circle of radius $1.27\\,a$"],["line","meridian","$\\phi$ constant, every $15°$"]],"turn":{"origins":[[0.0,0.0]],"meridians":24,"tint":{"star":"star","sheet":"cover"},"marks":[]}},"settings":"The first disc of the family at $m = a/5$, with the radius $a$ of the disc the unit of every length.","caption":["The plane $z = 0$ of the first Morgan-Morgan disc at one moment ($m = a/5$), drawn as a surface in flat space with every distance along it the metric distance. On it $g_{\\rho\\rho} = e^{2\\gamma - 2\\psi}$ and the circle of Weyl's radius $\\rho$ has circumference $2\\pi\\rho\\,e^{-\\psi}$, which is $2\\pi a\\,e^{3\\pi m/8a}$ at the rim.","The disc is a cap, smooth at its centre and steepest at the rim, where the dust moves at $0.94\\,c$, and the vacuum plane round it flattens with distance. The two meet at the rim with one tangent, and the curvature of the spacetime diverges there; the same plane at every moment is the same surface."]}]}
